\par
each iteration and iterating enough times to create an
\par
output distribution that offers a good approximation
\par
for making statistical inferences.(27) The quality of any
\par
approximation depends on how closely the input dis-
\par
tributions used match the true distributions and error
\par
decreases with increasing computational effort, which
\par
remains linear in the number of uncertain inputs and
\par
number of iterations.
