\par
These results suggest that general environmental
\par
health, toxicology, and clinical trial applications fo-
\par
cused primarily on societal-level policy decisions and
\par
the societal perspective. In contrast, the medical care
\par
applications focused almost exclusively on individual
\par
treatment decisions, although these split between the
\par
individual patient perspective and a societal perspec-
\par
tive. Finally, we observed that most water contamina-
\par
tion applications focused on firm-level decisions and
\par
firm perspective.
\par
The 4th section of Table 3 reports our findings re-
\par
lated to the decision analytic framework analysts used.
\par
Remarkably, all of the applications explicitly or implic-
\par
itly assumed risk neutrality for the DM. The medical
\par
applications most often used a cost-effectiveness analy-
