\par
DISCUSSION
\par
This analysis represents the first synthesis of VOI
\par
applications in health risk management. Overall, the
\par
literature adequately covers the basic components and
\par
methods of VOI analysis and illustrates the benefit of a
\par
VOI approach to inform research-planning decisions.
\par
However, we find a significant lack of cross-fertiliza-
\par
tion between fields, with analysts using different ter-
\par
minology, publishing in a wide variety of journals, and
\par
rarely citing applications in other fields. Not surpris-
\par
ingly, given the lack of cross-fertilization, this review
\par
shows that VOI analyses do not appear to follow a lin-
\par
ear progression. Instead, clusters of analysts tend to
\par
build on previous work within a field, but the progress
\par
does not necessarily spread widely even within the
\par
field. For example, in the water field, Reichard and Ev-
\par
ans54 explained the concept of EVPXI and included its
